              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "اوزار (auzār) is a loan, usually traced through Persian to Arabic awzār, the plural of wizr, \"a burden\", which Lane also gives as \"weapons, the gear of war\" (root w-z-r). Persian and Urdu use it for tools."
